WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
Your values are kind of like your inner cheerleader.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.500
They motivate you to do the things you care about.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.200
Your values represent what you think is most important in life.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.600
So let's take a closer look at that inner cheerleader.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.600
Now this is important.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.000
Why you ask?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.100
Because your values help shape all of your financial decisions.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.500
What material things are important to you?

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.900
How much money will you need?

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.000
And how will you earn that money?

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.200
Your values affect these decisions.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.700
But what influences our values?

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.900
Our family, teachers, and friends play a big role

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.600
in determining our values.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.400
Movies, music, and culture can make an impact too.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:41.000
Your value set is made up of a number of factors.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.300
Let's picture a big value web.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.400
Everyone's will look different.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.700
This is a big web.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.700
These values influence your financial decisions.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.600
Do you want a budget for a gym membership?

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.700
Own an electric bike or maybe a motorbike?

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.700
Do you want a budget for basketball tickets?

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.000
Or maybe you're a fan of the symphony?
